PRODUCTION INCIDENT – REAL WORLD DEVOPS 🚨

❓ Why was production slow even when everything looked healthy?
 ❓ Why were users complaining but dashboards were green?
 ❓ Why didn’t alerts trigger on time?

🔍 What actually went wrong in production:

 👉 Readiness probe was passing ✅
 👉 App was alive but thread pool was exhausted 🧵
 👉 Requests were queued, not failed ⏳
 👉 No alert for queue length ⚠️

💥 Impact:

 😤 Slow API responses
 📉 Drop in user experience
 🔥 Team panic during peak hours

🛠️ Solution implemented:

 ✅ Added thread-pool metrics 📊
 ✅ Alert on request queue length 🚨
 ✅ Updated readiness probe logic 🔁
 ✅ Load test before every release 🧪

📌 Production lesson:
 If you only monitor crashes 💀, you will miss slow failures 🐢.

This is the side of DevOps you learn only in production 🔥.
